# Reference for the environment variables this app reads. Fill in only
# if you want a real LLM instead of the built-in mock, or a database
# other than the default local SQLite file. The app runs completely
# fine with none of these set.
#
# NOTE: nothing in this project auto-loads a .env file - there is no
# python-dotenv dependency, deliberately, since the app needs no
# configuration at all to run. Copying this file to .env on its own does
# nothing; export the variables in your shell (or set them in whatever
# runs the process) before starting uvicorn:
#
#   export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...      # macOS / Linux
#   $env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY = "sk-ant-..."    # Windows PowerShell

# Comma-separated origins allowed to call this API cross-origin. Only
# needed if you serve frontend/index.html somewhere other than this app
# (which serves it at / by default, same origin, no CORS involved).
# CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5500

# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/lease_agent
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
